      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To determine the repeatability and response to therapy of dynamic contrast-enhanced (DCE) MRI biomarkers of synovitis in the hand and wrist of rheumatoid arthritis (RA) patients, and in particular the performance of the transfer constant K trans , in a multicentre trial setting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "DCE-MRI and RA MRI scoring (RAMRIS) were performed with meticulous standardisation at baseline and 6 and 24 weeks in a substudy of fostamatinib monotherapy in reducing synovitis compared with placebo or adalimumab. Analysis employed statistical shape modelling to avoid biased regions-of-interest, kinetic modelling and heuristic analyses. Repeatability was also evaluated."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "At early study termination, DCE-MRI data had been acquired from 58 patients in 19 imaging centres. K trans intra-subject coefficient of variation (N\u2009=\u200914) was 30%. K trans change demonstrated inferiority of fostamatinib (N\u2009=\u200911) relative to adalimumab (N\u2009=\u200910) after 6 weeks (treatment ratio\u2009=\u20091.92, p\u2009=\u20090.003), and failed to distinguish fostamatinib from placebo (N\u2009=\u200910, p\u2009=\u20090.79). RAMRIS showed superiority of fostamatinib relative to placebo at 6 weeks (p\u2009=\u20090.023), and did not distinguish fostamatinib from adalimumab at either 6 (p\u2009=\u20090.175) or 24 (p\u2009=\u20090.230) weeks."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "This demonstrated repeatability of K trans and its ability to distinguish treatment groups show that DCE-MRI biomarkers are suitable for use in multicentre RA trials."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "KEY POINTS",
          "content": "\u2022 DCE-MRI biomarkers are feasible in large multicentre studies of joint inflammation. \u2022 DCE-MRI K trans showed fostamatinib inferior to adalimumab after 6 weeks. \u2022 K trans repeatability coefficient of variation was 30% multicentre."
        }
      ]},
